{"id":783,"date":"2020-11-04T13:13:42","date_gmt":"2020-11-04T21:13:42","guid":{"rendered":"https:\/\/archive.learn.robolink.com\/?post_type=lesson&#038;p=783"},"modified":"2023-08-21T08:41:35","modified_gmt":"2023-08-21T15:41:35","slug":"led-3","status":"publish","type":"lesson","link":"https:\/\/archive.learn.robolink.com\/lesson\/led-3\/","title":{"rendered":"3A: LED"},"content":{"rendered":"<div class=\"wpb-content-wrapper\"><p>[vc_row][vc_column]<a id=\"6a22167825e33\" name=\"6a22167825e33\" class=\"scroll-spy-anchor\"><\/a>\n<div class=\"robolink-step \">\n\n\t\t<div class=\"robolink-step-head\"><span>Step 1<\/span><\/div>\n\t\n\t\t\t<h2>What is an LED?<\/h2>\n\t\n\t<p>[vc_column_text]<span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">LED stands for \u201clight-emitting diode\u201d. A diode is an electronic device that allows an electronic current to flow in only one direction. LEDs are beginning to replace traditional light bulbs because they are more efficient.<\/span><\/p>\n<p><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">Your CoDrone Mini has 1 RGB LED on the main body. RGB stands for red, green, and blue. Using the three colors, you can create almost every color imaginable! Aside from making your drone look cool, LEDs provide another form of feedback. A solid LED means your drone is connected, while a flashing LED means the battery is low or CDM is disconnected from the remote.<\/span>[\/vc_column_text]<\/p>\n<\/div>\n[\/vc_column][\/vc_row][vc_row][vc_column]<a id=\"6a22167825f94\" name=\"6a22167825f94\" class=\"scroll-spy-anchor\"><\/a>\n<div class=\"robolink-step \">\n\n\t\t<div class=\"robolink-step-head\"><span>Step 2<\/span><\/div>\n\t\n\t\t\t<h2>LED_color<\/h2>\n\t\n\t<p>[vc_column_text]<span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">The most basic LED function that you can use is LED_color. This will set your CoDrone Mini\u2019s LED to one color using the RGB colorspace. Don\u2019t worry &#8212; we\u2019ll get to that soon.<\/span><\/p>\n<p><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">This is what the function looks like:<\/span><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\"><br \/>\n<\/span><\/p>\n<pre class=\"EnlighterJSRAW\" data-enlighter-language=\"python\">LED_color(red, green, blue, brightness)<\/pre>\n<p><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">This is what each of the parameters means:<\/span><\/p>\n<ul>\n<li style=\"font-weight: 400;\"><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">Red, green, blue: an LED produces a color as a combination of red, green, and blue, or <\/span><b>RGB<\/b><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\"> for short. All of these values range from 0 to 255 corresponding to the color&#8217;s intensity, with 255 being the highest. For example, the RGB values for the color red correspond to (255,0,0). What are the RGB values for blue and green? What about purple? Use an RGB color picker like <\/span><a href=\"https:\/\/www.rapidtables.com\/web\/color\/RGB_Color.html\"><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">this one<\/span><\/a><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\"> to find out! Once you know what you want your LED\u2019s color to be, enter the RGB values into the corresponding spaces in the parentheses.<\/span><\/li>\n<li style=\"font-weight: 400;\"><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">Brightness: How bright the LEDs are, with 1 being off and 100 being maximum brightness. The brightness value will never be negative!<\/span><\/li>\n<\/ul>\n<p>[\/vc_column_text]<\/p>\n<\/div>\n[\/vc_column][\/vc_row][vc_row][vc_column]<a id=\"6a221678261d5\" name=\"6a221678261d5\" class=\"scroll-spy-anchor\"><\/a>\n<div class=\"robolink-step \">\n\n\t\t<div class=\"robolink-step-head\"><span>Step 3<\/span><\/div>\n\t\n\t\t\t<h2>Program a solid LED<\/h2>\n\t\n\t<p>[vc_column_text]<span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">Try this program out to see what a solid LED looks like. We programmed ours to show red, green, and blue, but you can use whatever colors you like.<\/span><\/p>\n<pre class=\"EnlighterJSRAW\" data-enlighter-language=\"python\">import CoDrone_mini\r\n\r\nimport time\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\ndrone = CoDrone_mini.CoDrone()\r\n\r\ndrone.pair()\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\ndrone.LED_color(255, 0, 0, 100)\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0# Red\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\r\n\r\ntime.sleep(1)\u00a0\r\n\r\ndrone.LED_color(0, 255, 0, 100). # Green\r\n\r\ntime.sleep(1)\r\n\r\ndrone.LED_color(0, 0, 255, 100). # Blue\r\n\r\ntime.sleep(1)<\/pre>\n<p><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">\u00a0<code class=\"EnlighterJSRAW\" data-enlighter-language=\"generic\">time.sleep()<\/code>\u00a0<\/span><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\"> is there to show each LED for 1 second before moving on to the next line of code. Change the sleep() parameter to show each color for a longer or shorter time.<\/span>[\/vc_column_text]<\/p>\n<\/div>\n[\/vc_column][\/vc_row][vc_row][vc_column]<a id=\"6a22167826458\" name=\"6a22167826458\" class=\"scroll-spy-anchor\"><\/a>\n<div class=\"robolink-step \">\n\n\t\t<div class=\"robolink-step-head\"><span>Step 4<\/span><\/div>\n\t\n\t\t\t<h2>LED_pattern()<\/h2>\n\t\n\t<p>[vc_column_text]<span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">If you think the solid LED function is too basic, we see you. The pattern LED function helps you set your CoDrone Mini\u2019s LED to both a color and one of three patterns. This is what it looks like:<\/span><\/p>\n<pre class=\"EnlighterJSRAW\" data-enlighter-language=\"python\">LED_pattern(red, green, blue, mode, speed)<\/pre>\n<p><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">This is what each of the parameters means:<\/span><\/p>\n<ul>\n<li style=\"font-weight: 400;\"><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">Red, green, blue: just like the solid LED function, this is where you set your LED\u2019s color using the RGB colorspace.<\/span><\/li>\n<li style=\"font-weight: 400;\"><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">Mode: also known as the pattern. You have three to choose from:<\/span>\n<ul>\n<li style=\"font-weight: 400;\"><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">BLINK flashes LED on and off<\/span><\/li>\n<li style=\"font-weight: 400;\"><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">DOUBLE BLINK flashes LED on twice before turning off<\/span><\/li>\n<li style=\"font-weight: 400;\"><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">PULSE turns LED on and off slowly<\/span><\/li>\n<li style=\"font-weight: 400;\"><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">FADE_IN increases the brightness of the LED from low to high<\/span><\/li>\n<li style=\"font-weight: 400;\"><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">FADE_OUT decreases the brightness of the LED from high to low<\/span><\/li>\n<\/ul>\n<\/li>\n<li style=\"font-weight: 400;\"><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">Speed: this is the speed of the LED\u2019s pattern. 1 is the slowest and 10 is the fastest. This value will never be negative! If you don\u2019t include this parameter, your program will use the default value, which is 5.<\/span><\/li>\n<\/ul>\n<p>[\/vc_column_text]<\/p>\n<\/div>\n[\/vc_column][\/vc_row][vc_row][vc_column]<a id=\"6a221678264ee\" name=\"6a221678264ee\" class=\"scroll-spy-anchor\"><\/a>\n<div class=\"robolink-step \">\n\n\t\t<div class=\"robolink-step-head\"><span>Step 5<\/span><\/div>\n\t\n\t\t\t<h2>Program a patterned LED<\/h2>\n\t\n\t<p>[vc_column_text]<span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">Try this program to see what the different LED programs look like. Again, we used red, green, and blue, but you can use whatever colors you like!<\/span><\/p>\n<p>&nbsp;<\/p>\n<pre class=\"EnlighterJSRAW\" data-enlighter-language=\"python\">import CoDrone_mini\r\n\r\nfrom CoDrone_mini import Mode\r\n\r\nimport time\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\ndrone = CoDrone_mini.CoDrone()\r\n\r\ndrone.pair()\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\ndrone.LED_pattern(255, 0, 0, Mode.BLINK, 10)\r\n\r\ntime.sleep(1)\r\n\r\ndrone.LED_pattern(0, 255, 0, Mode.DOUBLE_BLINK, 10)\r\n\r\ntime.sleep(1)\r\n\r\ndrone.LED_pattern(0, 0, 255, Mode.PULSE, 10)\r\n\r\ntime.sleep(1)\r\n\r\ndrone.close()<\/pre>\n<p>[\/vc_column_text]<\/p>\n<\/div>\n[\/vc_column][\/vc_row][vc_row][vc_column]<a id=\"6a2216782655f\" name=\"6a2216782655f\" class=\"scroll-spy-anchor\"><\/a>\n<div class=\"robolink-step \">\n\n\t\t<div class=\"robolink-step-head\"><span>Step 6<\/span><\/div>\n\t\n\t\t\t<h2>Other LED functions<\/h2>\n\t\n\t<p>[vc_column_text]<span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">If you\u2019re done with your LED or want to set it back to its default, there are two functions for that:<\/span><\/p>\n<ul>\n<li style=\"font-weight: 400;\"><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\"><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\"><code class=\"EnlighterJSRAW\" data-enlighter-language=\"generic\">turn_off_LED()<\/code><\/span><\/span><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">: turns the LED off. Perfect if you\u2019re trying to go undercover.<\/span><\/li>\n<li style=\"font-weight: 400;\"><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\"><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\"><code class=\"EnlighterJSRAW\" data-enlighter-language=\"generic\">reset_LED()<\/code>\u00a0<\/span><\/span><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">: resets the LED back to its default, which is solid red.<\/span><\/li>\n<\/ul>\n<p><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">Try using them at the end of one of your programs!<\/span>[\/vc_column_text]<\/p>\n<\/div>\n[\/vc_column][\/vc_row][vc_row][vc_column]<a id=\"6a22167826647\" name=\"6a22167826647\" class=\"scroll-spy-anchor\"><\/a>\n<div class=\"robolink-step \">\n\n\t\t<div class=\"robolink-step-head\"><span>Step 7<\/span><\/div>\n\t\n\t\t\t<h2>Adding flight movements<\/h2>\n\t\n\t<p>[vc_column_text]<span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">To add LEDs to a flight program, insert the LED functions where you want to see them in your program. The only exception is if you\u2019re setting your LED before takeoff. If you do this, you need to add <code class=\"EnlighterJSRAW\" data-enlighter-language=\"generic\">time.sleep(1)<\/code><\/span><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">right before your takeoff command so takeoff isn\u2019t skipped.<\/span><\/p>\n<pre class=\"EnlighterJSRAW\" data-enlighter-language=\"python\">import CoDrone_mini\r\n\r\nimport time\r\n\r\n\r\ndrone = CoDrone_mini.CoDrone()\r\n\r\ndrone.pair()\r\n\r\n\r\ndrone.LED_color(255, 0, 0, 100)\r\n\r\ntime.sleep(1) \u00a0 \u00a0 \u00a0 # Add a time.sleep(1) before takeoff if you're planning to set the LED cover before takeoff, otherwise the takeoff might get missed\r\n\r\ndrone.takeoff()\r\n\r\n\r\ndrone.set_throttle(50)\r\n\r\ndrone.move(1)\r\n\r\n\r\ndrone.LED_color(0, 255, 0, 100)\r\n\r\ndrone.set_yaw(50)\r\n\r\ndrone.move(2)\r\n\r\ndrone.LED_color(0, 0, 255, 100)\r\n\r\ndrone.set_yaw(50)\r\n\r\ndrone.move(2)\r\n\r\n\r\ndrone.land()\r\n\r\ndrone.close()<\/pre>\n<p>[\/vc_column_text]<\/p>\n<\/div>\n[\/vc_column][\/vc_row][vc_row][vc_column]<a id=\"6a221678266c1\" name=\"6a221678266c1\" class=\"scroll-spy-anchor\"><\/a>\n<div class=\"robolink-step \">\n\n\t\t<div class=\"robolink-step-head\"><span>Step 8<\/span><\/div>\n\t\n\t\t\t<h2>Challenge<\/h2>\n\t\n\t<p>[vc_column_text]<b>I Can See A Rainbow<\/b><\/p>\n<p><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">Draw a rainbow in the air with your CoDrone Mini! A rainbow has 6 colors (7 if you count indigo). There are a couple of ways to do this:<\/span><\/p>\n<ul>\n<li style=\"font-weight: 400;\"><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">Draw 6 or 7 different colored arcs<\/span><\/li>\n<li style=\"font-weight: 400;\"><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">Draw one long arc with a color for each section<\/span><\/li>\n<\/ul>\n<p>[\/vc_column_text]<\/p>\n<\/div>\n[\/vc_column][\/vc_row]<\/p>\n<\/div>","protected":false},"excerpt":{"rendered":"[vc_row][vc_column] Step 9 What is an LED? [vc_column_text]LED stands for \u201clight-emitting diode\u201d. A diode is an electronic device that allows an electronic current to flow in only one direction. LEDs&nbsp;<a href=\"https:\/\/archive.learn.robolink.com\/lesson\/led-3\/\">&hellip;<\/a>","protected":false},"featured_media":1730,"template":"","meta":{"_initial_content":"","_new_post":false,"_quiz_has_questions":false,"_lesson_complexity":"","_lesson_length":10,"_lesson_course":744,"_lesson_preview":"preview"},"lesson-category":[1782,1848,1793,1826,1482,853,694,59,171,63],"lesson-tag":[2135,2125,2120,2122,2134],"class_list":["post-783","lesson","type-lesson","status-publish","has-post-thumbnail","hentry","lesson-tag-beginner","lesson-tag-codrone-mini","lesson-tag-led","lesson-tag-programming","lesson-tag-python","module-beginner","post","odd"],"_links":{"self":[{"href":"https:\/\/archive.learn.robolink.com\/wp-json\/wp\/v2\/lessons\/783","targetHints":{"allow":["GET"]}}],"collection":[{"href":"https:\/\/archive.learn.robolink.com\/wp-json\/wp\/v2\/lessons"}],"about":[{"href":"https:\/\/archive.learn.robolink.com\/wp-json\/wp\/v2\/types\/lesson"}],"version-history":[{"count":5,"href":"https:\/\/archive.learn.robolink.com\/wp-json\/wp\/v2\/lessons\/783\/revisions"}],"predecessor-version":[{"id":2864,"href":"https:\/\/archive.learn.robolink.com\/wp-json\/wp\/v2\/lessons\/783\/revisions\/2864"}],"wp:featuredmedia":[{"embeddable":true,"href":"https:\/\/archive.learn.robolink.com\/wp-json\/wp\/v2\/media\/1730"}],"wp:attachment":[{"href":"https:\/\/archive.learn.robolink.com\/wp-json\/wp\/v2\/media?parent=783"}],"wp:term":[{"taxonomy":"lesson-category","embeddable":true,"href":"https:\/\/archive.learn.robolink.com\/wp-json\/wp\/v2\/lesson-category?post=783"},{"taxonomy":"lesson-tag","embeddable":true,"href":"https:\/\/archive.learn.robolink.com\/wp-json\/wp\/v2\/lesson-tag?post=783"}],"curies":[{"name":"wp","href":"https:\/\/api.w.org\/{rel}","templated":true}]}}